<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Our Indigenous Heritage – Lesson # 2</h2>
<p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 2</p></td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Reading</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</p></td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Indigenous Heritage</p></td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> Learning About Our Diverse Cultures</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Reading: Comprehend descriptive texts about places or events. Reading: Summarize the main points of different types of texts.</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can comprehend descriptive texts about Indigenous events in Panama (e.g., "The festival has two main events: the traditional dance and the cooking contest. It's a time for the community to come together").
Can summarize the main points of a text about Indigenous history (e.g., "Identify customs practiced at the Ngäbe-Buglé community." "Describe the beadwork used in Emberá traditional clothing." "List the types of dances performed during Guna Yala ceremonies.").
Can comprehend from descriptive texts details about Indigenous arts and crafts (e.g., "The Guna people use bright colors like red, yellow, and blue in their art.").</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <thead>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 34%; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a collage of images showcasing vibrant Indigenous arts and crafts from different Panamanian groups (e.g., Guna molas, Emberá beadwork, Ngäbe-Buglé chakaras). Students identify colors, patterns, and guess which group might be associated with each art piece. The teacher asks, "What do you see in these pictures?" and "Do you know which Indigenous group makes this art?"</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to extract simple information from a visual. For example, pointing to a mola, "This mola has very colorful patterns. It shows Guna traditions." The teacher emphasizes the pronunciation of "vibrant," "Indigenous," and "patterns."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Are these designs modern or traditional?" (Expected answer: Traditional.)</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do all these crafts look exactly the same, or are they diverse?" (Expected answer: Diverse.)</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Our Indigenous Heritage".</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short descriptive text (approx. 150-200 words) titled "The Vibrant Heritage of the Guna People." The text describes Guna traditions, art (molas), and ceremonies, incorporating present simple, past simple, adjectives, and target vocabulary (e.g., "Indigenous," "cultures," "traditions," "patterns," "vibrant," "colorful," "preserve," "community," "ceremony," "beadwork"). It could include phrases like, "The Guna people have preserved their traditions for centuries. Their molas are vibrant, colorful pieces of art. During ceremonies, the community comes together."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Reading comprehension of descriptive texts to understand details about Indigenous events, history, and arts.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Reading:</b> Students read the text silently and identify the main topic. Teacher asks: "What is this text mainly about?"</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False Statements:</b> Students read the text again and mark statements as true or false. (e.g., "Guna molas use only two colors." (False), "The Guna people value their ancestral traditions." (True)).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Detail Matching:</b> Students match specific descriptions from a list to their corresponding Guna cultural elements mentioned in the text (e.g., "Bright, layered fabric art" -> "Mola").</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Reading.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Reading for specific information, identifying vocabulary and grammar in context. Focus on present simple, past simple, adjectives for descriptions, and vocabulary (Indigenous, cultures, traditions, patterns, diversity, heritage, preservation, community, art, knowledge, ritual, ceremony, belief, land, family roots, cultural background, beadwork, vibrant, colorful, preserved, traditional, diverse, ancestral, cultural, historical).</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Vocabulary in Context (Controlled Practice):</b> Students receive a worksheet with sentences from "The Vibrant Heritage of the Guna People" text, but with target vocabulary words missing. They choose the correct word from a provided bank (e.g., "The Guna people ________ their rich cultural heritage through their art." Options: *preserve, migrate, discuss*).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Sentence Completion with Adjectives/Verbs (Semi-controlled):</b> Students complete sentences related to the text using appropriate adjectives or verbs from the vocabulary list, ensuring correct grammar (present simple/past simple). (e.g., "Guna molas are very ________ and unique." (colorful/vibrant)).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. <b>Reading Detail Scavenger Hunt (Pair Interaction/Peer Check):</b> In pairs, students re-read the text to find specific pieces of information. They receive a list of questions (e.g., "List two types of art mentioned in the text." "What is the Guna word for their layered fabric art?" "When did the Gunas migrate to their current lands, according to the text?") and highlight the answers in the text. Partners check each other's findings.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">12-15 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Our Indigenous Heritage".</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group "Indigenous Culture Fact Sheet" creation.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b> Students work in groups of 3-4. Each group's task is to create a "Fact Sheet" or a short digital poster (using a simple template or drawing) summarizing the main points and key details from "The Vibrant Heritage of the Guna People" text. They must include information about Guna art, traditions, community, and historical importance. They should use 3-5 key vocabulary words from the lesson (e.g., "Indigenous," "traditions," "colorful," "preserve," "community"). Encourage them to use descriptive adjectives (e.g., "vibrant patterns," "ancestral knowledge"). The final product is a concise summary of the text.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Theme/Scenario:</b> This activity directly applies the reading comprehension to share information about Indigenous heritage, promoting "Learning About Our Diverse Cultures." It reinforces acknowledging cultural value ("The Guna people's customs are unique and valuable").</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Reading for summary, collaboration, communicative task completion (creating a clear, informative fact sheet based on the text).</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation of group work and a quick review of the "Fact Sheets."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group briefly presents their "Fact Sheet" (1 minute per group, focusing on main points from their reading). Students also submit their written/typed summaries. This checks their ability to comprehend and summarize the text.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and accuracy of main points summarized from the text.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Inclusion of key details about Guna culture (e.g., specific art forms, events, historical aspects).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., Indigenous, traditions, vibrant, preserve, community).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaboration and contribution within the group.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation during the brief presentation, especially for multisyllabic words like "Indigenous," "identity," "vibrant."</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete an exit ticket with the following prompts:</p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new fact I learned about Indigenous cultures today is..."</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One word I found challenging to understand in the text was..."</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">6-8 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of the text was easiest for you to understand, and why?"</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can reading texts like this help us understand and respect our diverse cultures in Panama?"</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> What reading comprehension strategies worked best for students (e.g., highlighting, context clues)? Was the text level appropriate for A2.4? Did students effectively summarize the main points? What adjustments or scaffolds (e.g., pre-teaching more vocabulary, graphic organizers for summarizing) are needed for future reading lessons or for supporting students who struggled with summarization?</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 3, students will use the information they read and summarized today to engage in a speaking and interaction activity, discussing and sharing facts about Indigenous cultures in pairs and small groups, fostering the "sharing historical importance" pragmatic function and sociolinguistic discussions on preservation.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">2-3 min</p></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>